1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Three strong resumes. One open role. Find the evidence that matters.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Start with the job. Stay in one place. Add the title and description in quick start. Detailed setup is available when you need it.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Priorities when you need them. Suggested priorities are optional. Review and select the ones that matter to this search.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Add resumes. Start candidate review. Select resumes alongside the job description, then start the review. Assessments prepare as candidates finish.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Evidence first. Approval second. Review supported strengths, open questions, and proposed scores before applying them.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Direct evidence. Transferable experience. Inspect the inference, supporting passage, and question to verify. Confidence measures evidence support, not hiring success.

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
See what supports the assessment. Click a strength to open the resume and highlight the source passage.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,000
New feedback. A clearer picture. Alex triaged scanner findings. The manager clarifies that Alex did not implement the tools.

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Understand what changed—and why. blumr explains the new evidence and proposes an updated assessment. Current scores wait for approval.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Learning without extra steps. Eligible patterns from repeated, consistent feedback carry into relevant searches automatically. Custom lessons are optional.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
A more informed shortlist. Review the updated picture and decide who to speak with next.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
A concise draft. Ready for your edit. Prepare a short submittal built from the candidate’s supported strengths. Review, edit, and copy.

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Less time reviewing resumes. More time engaging the right people. Intelligence. Unlocked.
